## What Aescia changes operationally

Aescia does not replace clinical follow-up. It creates the structured visibility layer that makes follow-up scalable and consistent.

**What changes:**

- Each patient receives a daily structured check-in, configured to their pathway
- Responses are automatically assessed against clinician-authored rules
- Cases are classified by urgency — green (routine), amber (review), red (escalate)
- The clinical team sees a prioritized worklist each shift, not an uncontrolled alert queue
- Escalation is through existing site-defined pathways — Aescia does not prescribe the clinical response
- All check-in responses, classifications, and clinical actions are logged and auditable

**What does not change:**

- Clinical responsibility — this remains with the treating team at all times
- Escalation pathways — Aescia supports them, it does not replace them
- Governance and privacy requirements — Aescia is designed to operate within these

